SUMMARY:Screened to be Believed: The Jim Henson Company
DESCRIPTION:For more than 70 years\, The Jim Henson Company has delivered c
 ompelling stories and engaging world building that has captivated audience
 s for generations. By combining traditional puppetry arts with animatronic
 s and real-time digital animation\, the Company continues to be an unparal
 lelled leader in the fields of practical and special effects-based perform
 ance for stage and screen. Presented as part of the ‘Make\, Believe\, Ma
 gic: The Worlds of The Jim Henson Company’ exhibition (12 September 2026
  – 18 April 2027)\, ‘Screened to be Believed: The Jim Henson Company
 ’ showcases productions made by the Company that shine a light on the va
 st array of technical skills and artistry used to create unforgettable cin
 ematic worlds. Building from strong foundations laid by the Company’s fo
 unders\, The Jim Henson Company continues to foster a culture of innovatio
 n\, experimentation and exploration to forge new pathways in performance-l
 ed family entertainment\, making for some of the most memorable on-screen 
 moments in cinematic history. [sponsorLogos block] QAGOMA acknowledges the
  generous assistance of the National Film and Sound Archive of Australia\,
  Canberra and the NBCUniversal Archives & Collections\, Los Angeles in pro
 viding materials for this program. Program curated by Victoria Wareham\, A
 ustralian Cinémathèque with additional film note writing by Rebekah Bram
 mer.
LOCATION:GOMA\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
